cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use IP-Glasma, please cite the papers below: the original
  IP-Glasma papers and, if you use the JIMWLK evolution, the papers on its
  implementation.
title: IP-Glasma
type: software
abstract: >-
  IP-Glasma computes the initial state of heavy-ion and small-system
  collisions from the color-glass condensate: it samples the color charges
  of the colliding nuclei, builds their Wilson lines (optionally evolved in
  Bjorken x with JIMWLK) and evolves the gluon fields with the classical
  Yang-Mills equations, giving initial conditions for hydrodynamics,
  gluon spectra and eccentricities.
